        "text": "Each API request runs two checks (per user, per API key) as two Lua scripts on Redis. Redis capacity is drawn in checks per second: 80 primaries x 50,000 scripts/s / 2 scripts = 25,000 checks/s per primary. API server latency is only the limiter client's own work; the API's handler time is not part of this design."
